            <ArticleTitle>Splenosis presenting with adnexal mass: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>129-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE REPORT" NlmCategory="METHODS">A 21-year-old woman presenting with low abdominal discomfort, dysmenorrhoea and pelvic mass was misdiagnosed as endometriosis. She had post-traumatic splenic rupture and laparotomy history. RESULTS. Pelvic splenosis was diagnosed at laparotomy. Pelvic mass was removed and the other implants were left.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
